# Task file template (only this)

When writing or listing a Task.xxx, use **only** GitHub-flavored markdown with these headings. This is the format that is readable. Do not flatten it to unlabeled `.txt`. Do not use a FrontEnd “full step plan” list as the task file. Do not omit heading markers.

Specimen: `docs/tasks/Task.Docs.Pages.md`
Blank copy: `docs/tasks/Task.Template.md`

Required shape:

```markdown
# Task.Name

## Description

…

---

## Step Name.1 — short title

### Description

…

### Commands

- …

### Done When

- …
```

`#` = task name. `##` = task Description or a Step. `###` = Description, Commands, or Done When inside a step. Body text and bullets sit under those headings.

After the markdown exists, a canvas is optional follow-up only if Stacy asks.
